          "prompt": "MANDATORY: ONE SINGLE HORIZONTAL ROW of exactly four separate orthographic views of the SAME object, left to right: 1 FRONT view; 2 LEFT side view (object turned so its front points to the LEFT edge of the image); 3 BACK view; 4 RIGHT side view (object turned so its front points to the RIGHT edge of the image). Same scale and same ground line in all four, wide empty gaps between the views, every view complete and not cropped. Plain flat light neutral grey background (#D6D6D6). No floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no frames, no perspective, no extra objects. No fire, no smoke, no sparks, no lava, no glow halo: hot cracks, ember beds, flame tips and lantern glass are painted only as flat opaque bright orange-yellow colour areas.\n\nREFERENCE: the attached image is a crop of our approved scene concept. Redraw ONLY the bronze ding cauldron from it as a standalone game asset, keeping its shapes, proportions, materials and colours, simplified as described below; ignore everything else in the crop.\n\nSTYLE: stylized hand-painted 3D game environment asset: thick chunky silhouette that still reads as a solid black shape, broad clean faceted planes, two or three dominant colour blocks (warm aged bronze, dark brown-green patina, dark violet-grey basalt), soft painted gradients, a few medium-size ornaments, sparse wear, soot-darkened edges. No photorealism, no micro-grain, no fine brick seams, no dense cracks, no tiny carvings, no harsh highlights. Anything at ground level is basalt, stone or cast iron; timber only high up on buildings.\n\nOBJECT (7m wide x 8m tall x 6m deep): A giant ancient Chinese bronze ding cauldron: a deep round bowl-shaped belly 6m wide with a wide flat rim, two big upright square loop handles standing on the rim at the LEFT and RIGHT, and four thick short beast legs with clawed feet. The FRONT and the BACK of the belly each carry one big raised taotie monster face with broad simplified features (heavy brows, round eyes, fangs) and a band of large meander pattern under the rim. Warm aged bronze with dark brown-green patina in the recesses and soot at the bottom; the bowl is empty and dark inside. PROPORTIONS: FRONT and BACK views about 0.9 times as wide as tall; LEFT and RIGHT views about 0.75 times as wide as tall.",
