          "prompt": "KEY DESIGN: PINCHED WAIST + SIX 3D DRAGONS CLIMBING THE BELLY + OUTWARD-SPLAYED HANDLES. Not a plain round-bellied ding.\n\nMANDATORY: ONE SINGLE HORIZONTAL ROW of exactly four separate orthographic views of the SAME object, left to right: 1 FRONT view; 2 LEFT side view (object turned so its front points to the LEFT edge of the image); 3 BACK view; 4 RIGHT side view (object turned so its front points to the RIGHT edge of the image). Same scale and same ground line in all four, wide empty gaps between the views, every view complete and not cropped. Plain flat light neutral grey background (#D6D6D6). No floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no frames, no perspective, no extra objects. No fire, no smoke, no sparks, no lava, no glow halo: hot cracks, ember beds, flame tips and lantern glass are painted only as flat opaque bright orange-yellow colour areas.\n\nSTYLE: stylized hand-painted 3D game environment asset rooted in ancient Chinese culture of the southern Chu kingdom (Warring States, Hubei and Hunan): thick chunky silhouette that still reads as a solid black shape, broad clean faceted planes, two or three dominant colour blocks (warm aged bronze, dark green patina, soot), soft painted gradients, a few medium-size ornaments, sparse wear, soot-darkened edges. No photorealism, no micro-grain, no fine brick seams, no dense cracks, no tiny carvings, no harsh highlights. Anything at ground level is basalt, stone or cast iron; timber only high up on buildings.\n\nOBJECT (7m wide x 8m tall x 7m deep): A giant Chu-style bronze 'sheng ding' cauldron of southern China, modelled on the Wangzi Wu ding from Xichuan. SHAPE: a wide flat-bottomed bowl whose sides curve INWARD to a clearly PINCHED NARROW WAIST in the middle and flare out again to a wide flat rim, like a waisted drum; two big upright handles on the rim at the LEFT and RIGHT that splay strongly OUTWARD; three tall thick animal-hoof legs. CLIMBING DRAGONS: six chunky three-dimensional dragon-beasts climb up the outside of the belly, their bodies standing out from the surface and their heads peering over the rim (two on the FRONT, two on the BACK, one on each side). One broad band of interlaced dragon pattern at the waist, otherwise plain bronze. Warm aged bronze with dark green patina, soot near the feet; the bowl is empty. PROPORTIONS: FRONT and BACK views about 0.95 times as wide as tall; LEFT and RIGHT views about 0.85 times as wide as tall.",
